# DEFAULT. Gemini + OpenRouter + OpenCode: one provider pool per role, so a dry quota in one place does not stop
# the whole workflow, and builder / reviewer / tester are three different model families.
#
#   plan    Gemini API free tier   few requests, needs the best reasoning
#   build   OpenCode free          the heavy role (many tool calls): put it on the roomiest pool
#   review  OpenRouter free        few requests, so it fits OpenRouter's small shared quota
#   test    OpenCode free
#
# Needs the three providers connected in opencode. Check the exact IDs with `opencode models`.
# Notes (as of Nov 2026; these change often):
# - Gemini: gemini-4-hydrogen and gemini-3.8-flash have a free API tier; gemini-4-argon / gemini-4-carbon do not.
#   Google may use free-tier prompts to improve its products. If that matters for your code, set PLAN_MODEL to
#   opencode/deepseek-v4.1-flash-free (zero retention, no training).
# - OpenRouter: ALL :free models share one quota per account (20 req/min, 50 req/day; 1,000/day after buying $10 of
#   credits). That is why only the review role lives here. gemma-4-31b-it:free does not train on prompts.
#   Alternative that may train on prompts: openrouter/thinkingmachines/inkling-2-small:free
# - OpenCode: "free for a limited time". deepseek-v4.1-flash-free and glm-5.3-flash-free are zero-retention and do not
#   train. big-pickle, iceman-free, mimo-v2.6-flash-free, flint-40b-free and the nemotron free models may log or train:
#   avoid them for private code.
PLAN_MODEL=google/gemini-4-hydrogen
BUILD_MODEL=opencode/deepseek-v4.1-flash-free
REVIEW_MODEL=openrouter/google/gemma-4-31b-it:free
TEST_MODEL=opencode/glm-5.3-flash-free
